# Machine-managed DocOps surfaces are deliberately NOT `merge=union`.
# AUTO_INVENTORY.md carries a generated count block, while
# SOVEREIGN_MANIFEST.md carries both a generated active-track block and
# count-sensitive doctrine. A union merge can retain both sides of a managed
# block, silently duplicating rows or creating contradictory claims. Resolve
# conflicts explicitly and regenerate from owner inputs. The WP-0G amendment
# moves long-term volatile-count currentness to write-free, exact-SHA,
# non-authoritative projections; it does not make concatenation safe.

# High-churn prose docs: independently refreshed by multiple agents/PRs in short
# windows. `merge=union` prevents a hard conflict block — the result may need a
# quick cleanup pass to remove duplicate sections, but the PR is never stuck.
# Rule: only plain prose .md files here — never YAML, JSON, or code files where
# silent duplication would produce invalid content.

# State layer (morning brief + broken register): agents each write a full refresh.
docs/state/LIVE_OPS_DASHBOARD.md merge=union
docs/state/BROKEN_REGISTER.md merge=union

# Root orientation maps: updated by every spine-wiring / loop-closure PR.
CYBERNETIC_LOOP_MAP.md merge=union
INTERFACE_MISMATCH_MAP.md merge=union

# Governance evidence reports (active_track_evidence.*, track_portfolio.json,
# trust_gate_status.json) are no longer tracked — regenerated locally and
# published by CI to the generated/status branch — so they need no merge
# attribute at all.

# CLAUDE.md: deliberately NOT merge=union. It is updated by many governance,
# track-open, and coherence PRs, but it carries a machine-generated managed
# block (<!-- ACTIVE_TRACK:START --> … <!-- ACTIVE_TRACK:END -->) rendered by
# scripts/governance/render_active_track_includes.py and marked "Do not
# hand-edit". A union merge of two concurrent regenerations would keep BOTH
# copies, duplicating the block — exactly the invalid-content failure the rule
# above forbids. Resolve CLAUDE.md conflicts explicitly (or regenerate the
# block post-merge), keeping union merge for plain-prose docs only.
